WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.713
Chapter 11 puts the steps together
in a reference deployment.

2
00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:09.202
It's a framing pattern, not a real engagement:
a civilian agency with two forests,

3
00:00:09.202 --> 00:00:13.087
a trust between them, and a
fleet of SQL Server instances.

4
00:00:13.087 --> 00:00:16.200
The figures are illustrative;
the mechanics are real.

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.113
It runs in five phases.

6
00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:22.487
Discover: a read-only survey of
both forests, including the service

7
00:00:22.487 --> 00:00:27.576
accounts and every service principal
name the SQL Server work will depend on.

8
00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:32.750
Normalize: an organizational registry built
from that survey and checked against the

9
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.697
agency's own chart, with
a finding raised for every

10
00:00:35.697 --> 00:00:38.788
account the registry can't
attribute to a real owner.

11
00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:43.559
Map: one adapter per surface, and
four carry most of the risk here:

12
00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:47.688
synchronization, certificates,
RADIUS and SQL Server.

13
00:00:47.688 --> 00:00:51.147
Migrate: every change recorded
with who asked for it,

14
00:00:51.147 --> 00:00:54.526
on what authority, and a
hash of the resulting state.

15
00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:58.119
And Validate: the before and
after inventories compared,

16
00:00:58.119 --> 00:01:01.025
and every drift finding
closed with evidence.

17
00:01:01.025 --> 00:01:03.262
What comes out is an evidence bundle.

18
00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:07.377
It goes to the authorizing official
and the security control assessor,

19
00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:11.701
who authorize the agency's own system
under the Risk Management Framework.

20
00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.613
And it belongs to the agency.

21
00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:16.887
When the integrator leaves,
the registry, the schemas,

22
00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:21.620
the findings and the evidence stay
behind for the next authorization cycle.
